WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.490
In Kyoto, a Japanese browser gets
your TanStack Start page in English.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.090
The server renders this
English JSX for every request,

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.430
and nothing reads its language.

4
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.630
General Translation lets you translate a
TanStack Start app with gt-tanstack-start.

5
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.210
Install the experimental
gt-tanstack-start package,

6
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.030
and call initializeGT with
your languages and a loader.

7
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.130
Register gtMiddleware to
read each request's language,

8
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.370
and pass it from the
root route to GTProvider.

9
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.910
Wrap the page in T, sign in,
and run npx gt translate.

10
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.900
Now a Spanish browser
gets the page in Spanish,

11
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.250
and the one in Kyoto gets Japanese.
